{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implemented via TDD in worktree reb-2658-7032-docs; pushed as Gerrit change 1787.\n\nFinding 1 (correctness): outbound_differ create-path membership check made case-insensitive and now stamps the canonical mapping key (matches applier guard's uppercase normalization). Held-out RED test (lowercase 'b' vs key 'B' now creates + stamps 'B') verified RED before the fix, GREEN after, and returns to RED under the case-sensitive mutation.\n\nFinding 2 (tests): added end-to-end apply() test seeding projects.json — proves read_projects(repo_root) widens the guard scope (DIG allowed when seeded {REB,DIG}; ACME still refused). Characterizes already-correct wiring.\n\nFinding 3 (tests): added run_differs._run_differs_outbound seam test — malformed projects.json fails closed with ValueError. Characterizes already-correct fail-closed threading.\n\nFinding 4 (accepted): documented the two-read single-pass-window assumption in a code comment; no behaviour change.\n\nFull reconciler unit suite (2734) green; lint + typecheck clean."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786735301398648001,"uuid":"2e333a65-244e-4915-981e-e38f45d51e55"}